Autonomous Coaster Block Controller
Safety-Critical Ride Control & Attraction Automation System
Target Role: Theme Park Ride Control Systems & Controls Automation Engineer

1. System Abstract & Real-World Concept
In themed entertainment attractions, block zone safety systems guarantee the prevention of vehicle collisions by enforcing deterministic single-vehicle occupancy across track segments.
This block controller system implements a multi-tasking FreeRTOS framework on an ESP32 microcontroller to separate hard real-time safety interlocks from soft real-time observability telemetry. The system controls a station dispatch sequence using a high-speed PWM servo actuator (simulating station brake fins/restraint lock arms), dual operator control inputs (Emergency Stop and Station Dispatch buttons), and closed-loop speed monitoring with automated overspeed fault injection.

